\section{Big Idea, Essential Question and Challenge}

\subsection{Big Idea}
\begin{quote}
\textbf{Trust in reimbursement decisions.} Fraud, waste and abuse should be stopped before money leaves the insurer, and defences should be tested against fraud that has not happened yet.
\end{quote}

\subsection{Essential Question}
\begin{quote}
\emph{How can healthcare insurers make fair and trustworthy reimbursement decisions while distinguishing legitimate care from suspicious behaviour?}
\end{quote}

\subsection{Challenge}
\begin{quote}
\emph{A model trained on recoveries only learns from fraud that already happened. Can an AI invent new fraud strategies against our own defences, so that the holes are patched before a real person finds them?}
\end{quote}

The challenge turns a broad question about fairness and trust into something that can be built and measured: an attacker agent, a defender model, and a measurable \emph{attack success rate} before and after the defender is strengthened.

