\subsection{Why adversarial self-play?}
As Table~\ref{tab:gaps} shows, the implementation addresses the \emph{adaptation} side of G2 and contributes regional evidence for G5; G1, G3 and G4 remain open (Chapter~\ref{ch:future}). With two months, one solution had to be built in depth. Adversarial self-play was chosen because it answers the stated challenge directly, builds on the pipeline and detector already produced, gives a measurable result (attack success before and after retraining) and targets the weakness identified above: detectors trained on history cannot anticipate adaptation.


