\section{Step 1: Feature Set and Encoder (\texttt{common.py})}\label{sec:defv1}

\subsection{Why not reuse the 109-column pipeline}
The RL environment must cheaply re-score a claim every time the agent changes its claimed amount, possibly hundreds of thousands of times across training. That requires knowing exactly how every input was built so that the amount-dependent ones can be recomputed per step without re-deriving the whole encoding pipeline. The frequency encodings and peer or provider aggregates of \texttt{claims\_ml\_ready.csv} were fitted on the whole dataset and cannot be recomputed at this granularity.

