\section{Step 6: Retraining the Defender (\texttt{defender\_v2})}\label{sec:retrain}
The agreed MVP stopped at ``single agent against a static defender''. This step goes one round further. It is a single-round taste of the proposal's co-evolution loop: feed the discovered attacks to the defender and retrain.

\begin{enumerate}[nosep]
  \item Run the trained policy on evaluation episodes and save the \textbf{successful evasive sub-claims}: 337 of them.
  \item Label them as fraud (1) and add them to the real training data: 252 original positives + 337 adversarial positives = \textbf{589 positives}, on top of the same negatives.
  \item Retrain XGBoost with the \emph{same hyperparameters} as \texttt{defender\_v1}, producing \texttt{defender\_v2}.
  \item \textbf{Do not retrain the PPO agent.} Re-evaluate the \emph{same frozen policy} against \texttt{defender\_v2}, which isolates the effect of the defender's improvement.
\end{enumerate}

